id: ops-cl0o
title: "Adding a source file breaks the coverage gate in three places, and none of them says so"
description: "The coverage gate enumerates every source file so that a file added without tests cannot pass by being absent from the report. That enumeration is duplicated by hand in three fixture lists inside test/coverage-gate.test.ts (a POSIX stub, a Windows stub, and an explicit array) plus the include list in the package coverage script. Adding one source file therefore requires four coordinated edits, and omitting any of them fails the gate with a coverage threshold error that names a percentage rather than the missing file. Two source files added in this session each hit it."
type: Issue
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags[3]: "area:release","area:testing","type:defect"
created_at: "2026-08-28T14:25:04.891Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-29T20:12:56.601Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: New TypeScript modules require no edits to hard-coded coverage fixture lists; overlapping source roots produce a sorted unique required-file denominator; real c8 accepts a newly tested module and rejects an unimported module by filename at unchanged per-file 100/100/100/100 thresholds; CLI/SDK 2026.9.29 and the lockfile pass package release checks; required exact-head reviews complete before merge; Every c8 invocation uses the measured repositorys coverage/tmp directory and preserves an enclosing coverage run
definition_of_ready: Canonical pm-ops checkout and tracker verified; no other claim or active checkout process; stacked on the existing TSX gate candidate
risk: low
blocked_by: ops-0c8k
blocked_reason: Full internal documentation gate remains incomplete under ops-0c8k. Parent PR132 and new exact-head substantive reviews remain required. Default CI omits two opt-in real-fleet checks; Trivy and ShellCheck are unavailable locally.
repro_steps: Configure overlapping coverageGate.sources entries and run node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts. A nested c8 invocation previously inherited and cleaned the enclosing raw-counter directory.
expected_result: "New source modules are discovered once in deterministic order without fixture list edits, while nested coverage invocations preserve parent data and all required measured gates remain enforced."
actual_result: "Source roots are deduplicated and sorted, controlled reports follow include arguments, real c8 rejects unimported modules by filename, and repository-owned counter directories preserve parent data."
